Keycloak webhook event listener, identity-sync fork

This folder is a modified copy of sashyo/keycloak-webhook-listener.
Source: https://github.com/sashyo/keycloak-webhook-listener
Commit: 5f23e5530db15c9042d8977c46a19758aa0ede97 (23 October 2026)
The upstream project has no NOTICE file. Its license is the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The license text is in the LICENSE file next to this one.

Changes made by this project:
- The request is signed as the identity-sync contract asks: headers X-Identity-Sync-Timestamp and
  X-Identity-Sync-Signature, HMAC-SHA256 over "<timestamp>.<mode>.<raw body>" (WebhookSigner).
- The body is Keycloak's own event format with realmId. Only the event types identity-sync
  processes are sent. IP address, details and representation are not sent (EventPayloads).
- A failed delivery is retried at most three times. Each attempt has a new timestamp (WebhookSender).
- Keycloak 26.8.2 and Java 21. JUnit tests were added.
